+The crop proxy is an illustrative account construction. We combine independently sourced OWID/FAOSTAT world cropland area, defined as arable plus permanent-crop area (ha), with cereal yield (tonnes per hectare) \citep{OWIDCropland2026,OWIDCereal2026}. Cereal yield is a productivity indicator, not a measure of output from all crops. For a declared 1961 account-share anchor $\phi_0$, we set $\hat b_f(t)=\hat b_f(1961)\tilde b_f(t)/\tilde b_f(1961)$, with $\hat b_f(1961)A_f(1961)=\phi_0B(1961)$. We then define $X_t=\hat b_f(t)A_f(t)$ and $C^{\mathrm{emp}}_t=B_t-X_t$. Thus $X$ is an index-scaled account proxy, and $C^{\mathrm{emp}}$ is the residual that reconciles it to the NFA total. The residual is not observed ecological capital, non-cropland biocapacity, or the model quantity $\Ups(q)A_c$.
+
+When both $X$ and $C^{\mathrm{emp}}$ are positive at the two endpoints, the exact log-mean Divisia identity is
 \begin{equation}
-\Delta\ln B=w_X\bigl(\Delta\ln\tilde b_f+\Delta\ln A_f\bigr)+w_C\Delta\ln C,
-\qquad w_X=\frac{L(X_T,X_0)}{L(B_T,B_0)},\quad w_C=\frac{L(C_T,C_0)}{L(B_T,B_0)},
+\Delta\ln B=w_X\bigl(\Delta\ln\tilde b_f+\Delta\ln A_f\bigr)+w_C\Delta\ln C^{\mathrm{emp}},
+\qquad w_X=\frac{L(X_T,X_0)}{L(B_T,B_0)},\quad w_C=\frac{L(C^{\mathrm{emp}}_T,C^{\mathrm{emp}}_0)}{L(B_T,B_0)},
 \end{equation}
 Here $L(a,b)=(b-a)/(\ln b-\ln a)$ is the logarithmic mean, with its continuous limit when $a=b$. We use the measured 1961 NFA cropland share, $\phi_0=0.1286472202$, as the central anchor. Mapping that account share to the external area--yield proxy is an assumption, not an independent observation of physical capital. Table~\ref{tab:si_phi0} gives the selected sensitivity for 1961--2023. At the central anchor, the cereal-yield, area, and residual terms are $+0.268662$, $+0.037710$, and $-0.084375$, summing to $\Delta\ln B=+0.221997$. The same-edition 1961--2022 sensitivity gives $+0.264696$, $+0.037506$, and $-0.082705$, summing to $+0.219497$. The decomposition is exact for this proxy, but its allocation depends on $\phi_0$ and is not a physical-stock attribution.
 
